window.HS_INDEX = [{"lang":"zh","path":"account/language","title":"界面语言","headings":["界面语言","支持的语言","切换","三个概念不要混","相关页面"],"text":"界面语言 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 界面语言 界面语言只影响按钮、提示这些站点文案，不影响书籍内容。 支持的语言 简体中文、繁體中文、English、日本語、한국어、Deutsch、Español、Français。 切换 在阅读设置面板里找到「界面语言」分区；登录页与落地页上也有语言选择入口。 选择语言后，界面文案立即切换。 刷新后仍保持你选择的语言。 三个概念不要混 概念影响什么 界面语言按钮、菜单、提示等站点文案 书的语言书本身的内容，不会被界面语言改变 翻译目标语言AI 翻译把书译成哪种语言 相关页面 阅读设置总览 翻译范围与语言"},{"lang":"zh","path":"account/profile","title":"个人资料与密码","headings":["个人资料与密码","修改资料","修改密码","登录状态异常","相关页面"],"text":"个人资料与密码 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 个人资料与密码 账号相关设置集中在个人资料页。 修改资料 登录后打开个人资料页。 修改密码，邮箱等基本信息。 保存后立即生效。 修改密码 在个人资料页找到密码区域。 输入当前密码与新密码，提交。 下次登录使用新密码。 忘记当前密码时，走登录页的「忘记密码」流程。 登录状态异常 长时间未使用后，可能会提示登录已过期，重新登录即可。 阅读进度、书签、笔记都跟着账号保存，重新登录后仍在。 如果浏览器禁用了 Cookie，登录状态可能无法保持。 相关页面 注册与登录 界面语言 故障排除"},{"lang":"zh","path":"ai/chat","title":"基于本书提问","headings":["基于本书提问","打开对话","适合问什么","回答里的依据","怎么用","两种标记分别表示什么","为什么有时只有边框、没有黄底","相关页面"],"text":"基于本书提问 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 基于本书提问 AI 会先在当前这本书里找相关内容，再据此回答，而不是用通用知识泛泛而谈。 打开对话 打开一本书。 点工具栏的「AI 对话」，右侧打开对话面板。 在输入框里提问并发送。 适合问什么 总结：「这一章主要讲了什么？」 解释：「这里说的 X 是什么意思？」 定位：「书里第一次提到 Y 是在哪里？」 对比：「作者对 A 和 B 的看法有什么不同？」 追问：针对上一条回答继续问，不必重复背景。 回答里的依据 回答中带编号的角标就是引用。每个回答都会标明它的依据来自书里的哪一段，你可以点回去自己核对。 怎么用 在 AI 对话里提问，等待回答完成。 点击任意一个角标。 阅读器会跳到对应的章节与段落，并把引用位置标出来。 两种标记分别表示什么 标记含义 黄色边框 回答引用的那一段。用来告诉你「依据在这里」。 黄色底色 答案里确实逐字使用了的原文句子。用来告诉你「具体是这几句话」。 为什么有时只有边框、没有黄底 如果 AI 是概括或改写了段落的意思，原文里就没有被完整使用的句子，此时只会标出整段。这说明引用的是这一段的含义，而不是某一句话。 相关页面 会话管理 配额与用量"},{"lang":"zh","path":"ai/quota","title":"配额与用量","headings":["配额与用量","用量怎么算","额度用尽时","怎么省着用","相关页面"],"text":"配额与用量 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 配额与用量 系统会提供少量 token 用于试用 AI 翻译与 AI 对话；也可以填入自己的大模型 API Key（BYOK）。 用量怎么算 翻译与对话都会消耗额度，消耗量取决于处理了多少文字。 整书翻译 ＞ 当前章 ＞ 跟随阅读，范围越大消耗越多。 普通阅读、书签、笔记、搜索不消耗额度。 额度用尽时 发起新的 AI 请求会收到提示，说明本月额度已用完。 已经译好的内容、已经完成的对话不受影响，仍然可以看。 最好的办法是用你自己的 API Key（BYOK）。 怎么省着用 先用「跟随阅读」看几段，确认译文质量再考虑整书。 只是想弄懂一句话时，用划词翻译，比整章翻译省得多。 同一个问题不要反复重问；需要补充时就着上一轮追问。 相关页面 翻译范围与语言 基于本书提问"},{"lang":"zh","path":"ai/sessions","title":"会话管理","headings":["会话管理","新建","历史","小建议","相关页面"],"text":"会话管理 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 会话管理 每次围绕一本书的连续提问属于同一个会话。换话题时建议新建会话，回答会更聚焦。 新建 在对话面板里点「新建会话」，之后的问题都归到这个会话里。 历史 面板里列出这本书的历史会话，按时间排序，最近的在前。 点任意一条即可切换过去，继续之前的对话。 时间显示为「刚刚」「N 分钟前」「N 小时前」「N 天前」。 小建议 一个会话只围绕一个主题，回答会更准确。 会话按书分开，换了书也不会串。 相关页面 基于本书提问 配额与用量"},{"lang":"zh","path":"faq/index","title":"常见问题","headings":["常见问题","通用","需要注册才能用吗？","我的数据存在哪里？","支持哪些浏览器？","需要自己准备 AI 的 API Key 吗？","书籍与格式","支持哪些格式？","能读有 DRM 保护的书吗？","为什么 PDF 显示效果不理想？","上传有大小限制吗？","AI 功能","翻译要等多久？","为什么有的引用只有边框、没有黄底？","AI 额度用完了怎么办？","还有问题？"],"text":"常见问题 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 常见问题 通用 需要注册才能用吗？ 不需要。系统支持匿名访问，浏览、阅读、进度、书签和笔记都照常保存。 我的数据存在哪里？ FacetShelf 是在线服务，书库信息、阅读进度、书签、笔记与 AI 会话保存在站点的服务器上，不在本地。上传的私有书只有你自己能看到。 支持哪些浏览器？ 建议使用较新版本的 Chrome、Edge、Firefox 或 Safari。双列对照等布局在电脑上效果最好。 需要自己准备 AI 的 API Key 吗？ 系统会提供少量 token 用于试用 AI 翻译与 AI 对话；也可以填入自己的大模型 API Key（BYOK）。 书籍与格式 支持哪些格式？ EPUB、MOBI、AZW3、PDF、TXT 格式。 能读有 DRM 保护的书吗？ 不能。带 DRM 的电子书无法解析。 为什么 PDF 显示效果不理想？ PDF 是固定版式，解析起来比较困难，目前只能按原版式预览。将来可能会提供PDF的流式重排功能。 上传有大小限制吗？ 有。单文件大小与一次批量上传的数量取决于账号档位，超出时会在上传前提示。 AI 功能 翻译要等多久？ 取决于范围：跟随阅读几乎即时；整章需要一点时间；整书最久。可以边读边等，已译好的部分会先显示。 为什么有的引用只有边框、没有黄底？ 说明 AI 引用的是那一段的意思，做的是概括或改写，原文里没有被逐字使用的句子。详见基于本书提问。 AI 额度用完了怎么办？ 当月额度用完后，新的 AI 请求会提示额度不足；阅读、书签、笔记不受影响，已译好的内容仍可查看。详见配额与用量。 还有问题？ 看看故障排除，或通过站点页脚的「联系」告诉我们。"},{"lang":"zh","path":"faq/troubleshooting","title":"故障排除","headings":["故障排除","打不开书","译文没有出现","AI 没有响应","登录状态丢失","页面显示的还是旧内容","还是没解决"],"text":"故障排除 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 故障排除 打不开书 先刷新页面重试一次。 确认这本书是 EPUB、PDF、MOBI、AZW3 或 TXT。 如果是刚上传的书，等上传进度走完再打开。 大文件首次打开会比较慢。 译文没有出现 确认「AI 翻译」分区里已经选了翻译模式（不是「关闭」）。 确认目标语言与书的语言不同。 「跟随阅读」只在读到的地方翻译，往回翻到已译部分才会显示。 检查是否提示额度不足。 AI 没有响应 看是否提示额度已用完。 稍等片刻再试，或换一个更短的问题。 如果长时间无响应，刷新页面后重新提问。 登录状态丢失 重新登录即可，阅读数据不会丢。 如果反复失效，检查浏览器是否禁用了 Cookie 或处于无痕模式。 同一账号在多处频繁切换登录时，可能出现会话失效提示。 页面显示的还是旧内容 按下 Ctrl + F5 强制刷新，可以跳过浏览器缓存。 还是没解决 请通过站点页脚的「联系」告诉我们：哪本书、在哪个页面、做了什么操作、看到什么提示。"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/annotations","title":"笔记与标注","headings":["笔记与标注","菜单里的操作","五种颜色","笔记","关闭弹出菜单","相关页面"],"text":"笔记与标注 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 笔记与标注 在正文里选中文字，会弹出一个操作菜单。 菜单里的操作 操作作用 拷贝复制选中的文字 笔记为选中的文字添加一条笔记 书签把这段文字标为书签 马克笔给文字加底色 直线 / 波浪线在文字下方画线 搜索用选中的文字在书内搜索 翻译翻译选中的文字 AI就选中的文字向 AI 提问 五种颜色 菜单下方一排是颜色：红、紫、蓝、绿、金。新建标注默认用哪一种，可以在阅读设置的「书签与标注」分区里改。 笔记 选中文字点「笔记」，在弹出框里写内容后保存。 笔记可以在书签面板里查看；预览方式（悬停或点击）可以在设置里改。 已有笔记可以再次打开修改或删除。 关闭弹出菜单 如果不想每次选中文字都弹出菜单，可以把「选区操作弹窗」设为「右键」或「关闭」。 相关页面 书签 阅读设置总览 划词翻译"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/appearance","title":"外观与主题","headings":["外观与主题","字体与字号","颜色与背景","自定义 CSS","明暗主题","相关页面"],"text":"外观与主题 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 外观与主题 外观设置只改变显示方式，不会改动书的内容和文件。 字体与字号 字体：可选内置字体或「书默认」。使用本机字体时，浏览器可能会询问权限。 字号：整体放大或缩小正文。 行距 / 字距 / 段间距：分别控制行与行、字与字、段落之间的距离。 颜色与背景 文字颜色：支持十六进制（如 #333333）或 rgb(...)。 背景颜色：支持 #rrggbb 或 rgba(...)，留空则「跟随原书」。 背景图片：填写一个 CSS 背景图地址。 留空表示「跟随原书」，不会强行覆盖。 自定义 CSS 熟悉 CSS 的话，可以进一步调整正文样式，例如首行缩进： p { text-indent: 2em; } 不熟悉的话保持留空即可。 明暗主题 快捷工具条上有一个明暗切换按钮，切换的是阅读器界面的主题。它与上面的背景色是两件事：主题管界面，背景色管正文。 相关页面 阅读设置总览 阅读配置档"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/bookmarks","title":"书签","headings":["书签","添加书签","查看与跳转","排序与分页","与标注的区别"],"text":"书签 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 书签 书签记录的是位置，用来快速回到某处继续读。 添加书签 翻到想记住的位置。 点阅读区上方快捷工具条里的「加书签」。 当前页面（连续模式下是当前位置）会被记下。 查看与跳转 点左侧工具栏的「书签」打开书签面板。 面板里会列出这本书的全部书签。 点任意一条，正文跳到该位置。 排序与分页 书签可以按时间或按在书中的位置排序，点击面板上的两个排序按钮（按加入时间 / 按位置）。 书签较多时分页显示；每页条数可在阅读设置的「面板」分区里调整。 与标注的区别 书签只记位置；如果要对某段文字做标记或写笔记，用笔记与标注。"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/modes","title":"四种阅读模式","headings":["四种阅读模式","四种模式","怎么切换","相关页面"],"text":"四种阅读模式 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 四种阅读模式 阅读器提供四种排版方式。它们只影响页面怎么排列，不影响书的内容。 四种模式 模式显示方式适合 全书连续模式 全书连续滚动，同时显示多个章节 长时间阅读、习惯上下滚动的读者 单章连续 每次只显示一个章节，章内滚动 想按章推进、又不想左右翻页 单页 一次显示一页，向左右翻页 接近纸书的翻页感 双页 一次并排显示两页 大屏幕，或想同时看到前后内容 怎么切换 打开任意一本书，进入阅读器。 在左侧工具栏点「单页模式」「双页模式」「连续模式」或「单章连续模式」。 阅读设置面板的「布局」分区里还有更细的选项，例如到章边界时是否自动换章。 切换模式后，阅读位置会尽量保持在原来的位置；分页模式与滚动模式之间换算时，可能落在相邻的一页。 相关页面 翻页与定位 阅读设置总览 外观与主题"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/navigate","title":"翻页与定位","headings":["翻页与定位","翻页","换章","继续上次的位置","调整宽度与留白","相关页面"],"text":"翻页与定位 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 翻页与定位 两种移动方式：连续模式下滚动，分页模式下翻页。到了章的边界会接着进入下一章。 翻页 分页模式：点正文中线的左侧或右侧翻页；也可以用方向键、PageUp / PageDown、空格（Shift+空格往前）。 连续模式：直接上下滚动。 换章 到章末再往下翻，会进入下一章；到章首往回翻，会进入上一章。 「边界换章」可以选择自动或手动：自动是翻到边界继续就换章；手动需要你明确触发。 往回翻进入上一章时，「上翻落点」可以选择停在章首还是章末。 继续上次的位置 打开一本书时，默认回到上次读到的地方。如果希望每次都从第一页开始，可以在阅读设置的「阅读行为」里关闭「记忆上次阅读位置」。 调整宽度与留白 快捷工具条上的「宽度」可以调正文宽度，点「推荐」回到建议比例。 分页模式下还可以分别调上下留白。 相关页面 四种阅读模式 阅读设置总览"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/offline","title":"离线阅读","headings":["离线阅读","开启","下载整本书","断网时","离线时不能用的","缓存与清理","相关页面"],"text":"离线阅读 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 离线阅读 离线阅读的目的是确保离线时能继续阅读。 在设置中开启离线阅读。你之后阅读的章节会自动缓存；也可以手动下载整本书，把全部章节缓存下来。 开启 在阅读器里打开工具栏的「设置」面板（各分区说明见 阅读设置总览）。 展开「阅读行为」分区。 把「离线阅读」设为开启。默认是关闭的。 开启后，阅读器右下角出现「离线下载」按钮；关闭后按钮隐藏，离线缓存也不再接管页面请求。 下载整本书 点右下角的「离线下载」，开始缓存整本书：各章正文、目录、封面和书籍信息。 下载期间显示进度条；完成后短暂显示「离线完成 ✓」，随后按钮恢复原状。 想更新缓存时，再点一次即可重新下载。 不点下载也能离线读，但只限于这台设备上打开过的章节；点一次「离线下载」才会把整本书补齐。 断网时 右下角出现「离线模式」标记。 已下载的书可以照常打开、翻章、跳目录。 没下载的书，或书里还没缓存的章节，会提示这一章尚未缓存；联网后再进入即可。 离线时不能用的 AI 翻译、AI 对话、划词翻译等需要联网的功能。 离线读到的是原文，译文要联网才能生成。 缓存与清理 下载的内容保存在当前这台设备的浏览器里，换设备需要重新下载。 缓存不跟账号走：登录、退出登录、切换账号或者登录状态过期时，本设备已下载的书会被清空，需要重新下载。 应用里没有「删除缓存」的按钮。把「离线阅读」设为关闭只停止离线缓存的接管，已下载的内容仍然留在浏览器里；要彻底清除，请使用浏览器的「清除站点数据」。 相关页面 阅读设置总览 翻页与定位 故障排除"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/profiles","title":"阅读配置档","headings":["阅读配置档","默认档","另存为","切换与删除","常见用法","相关页面"],"text":"阅读配置档 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 阅读配置档 一套完整的阅读设置就是一个配置档。你可以为不同场景准备多套，随时切换。 默认档 每一处设置的改动都会自动存进名为 default 的配置档。 default 不能删除。 另存为 先把各项设置调到你想要的状态。 在「阅读配置」分区里输入一个名字，点「另存为」。 这套设置就成为一个独立的配置档。 如果名字已存在，会询问是否覆盖。 切换与删除 在下拉里选中某个配置档，它的设置会立即应用。 删除配置档前会确认，删除后不可恢复。 要修改已保存的配置档：选中它 → 调整设置 → 用同名再存一次。 常见用法 一套白天阅读（浅色背景、大字号），一套夜间阅读（深色、行距更宽）。 一套专用于双列对照翻译时的宽度。 相关页面 阅读设置总览 外观与主题"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/settings","title":"阅读设置总览","headings":["阅读设置总览","八个分区","保存与恢复","相关页面"],"text":"阅读设置总览 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 阅读设置总览 点工具栏的「设置」打开面板。改动立即生效，并自动保存。 八个分区 分区管什么 阅读配置配置档的选择、另存与删除 布局各模式的宽度，以及分页模式的上下留白 外观字体、字号、颜色、背景、行距、字距、段间距、自定义 CSS 阅读行为明暗主题、阅读模式、记忆上次阅读位置、边界换章、翻页动画、离线阅读、选中弹出 书签与标注新建标注的默认颜色、笔记预览方式 面板书签与搜索结果的每页条数 AI 模型AI 翻译与 AI 对话共用的 AI 服务 AI 翻译翻译模式、范围、译文主题、源语言与目标语言 保存与恢复 所有改动立即保存到当前配置档，不需要点「保存」。 改动只影响阅读器，不会改动书本身的文件。 想保留多套设置，用 阅读配置档。 相关页面 外观与主题 翻页与定位 三种翻译排版"},{"lang":"zh","path":"reading/toc-search","title":"目录与书内搜索","headings":["目录与书内搜索","目录","书内搜索","结果分页","相关页面"],"text":"目录与书内搜索 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 目录与书内搜索 目录用来跳章，搜索用来找具体的一句话。 目录 点工具栏的「显示/隐藏目录」，右侧会打开章节列表。 点击任意一章，正文会跳到该章开头。 再点一次「显示/隐藏目录」可以收起面板。 书内搜索 点工具栏的「搜索」，在面板里输入关键词并回车。可以输入多个关键词，用空格分隔，表示「与」关系。 结果按章节列出，显示命中的文字片段。 点一条结果，跳到对应位置，命中的文字会标出来。 结果分页 结果较多时分页显示。每页显示多少条可以在阅读设置的「面板」分区里调整，默认按面板高度自动适配。 相关页面 书签 阅读设置总览"},{"lang":"zh","path":"shelf/facets","title":"目录、分类与标签","headings":["目录、分类与标签","三类入口","筛选","配合搜索","相关页面"],"text":"目录、分类与标签 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 目录、分类与标签 书架左侧的目录树有三个来源，用来快速把书库缩小到你要找的范围。 三类入口 入口说明 来源书来自哪个书库或目录 分类按主题归类，由站点或你自己维护 标签更灵活的关键词，一本书可以有多个 筛选 展开左侧目录树，点开对应的分类或标签。 书架只显示属于该项的书，顶栏会提示当前的筛选条件与数量。 要取消筛选，点顶栏筛选条件旁的 ×，或回到「全部」。 配合搜索 在某一分类或标签下使用搜索框，只会在当前范围内查找。 相关页面 书架与视图 上传书籍"},{"lang":"zh","path":"shelf/llm-provider","title":"AI 模型设置","headings":["AI 模型设置","在哪里","添加一个模型","字段","测试连接与拉取模型","修改与删除","和翻译、AI 对话的关系","关于密钥","相关页面"],"text":"AI 模型设置 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 AI 模型设置 AI 翻译和 AI 对话都需要一个大模型服务。可以在这里填入自己的 API Key，按自己的账号和额度调用。 在哪里 打开书架。 在左侧工具栏点「设置」。 右侧面板里找到「AI 模型」。 添加一个模型 点「+ 添加」。 选择「类型」，填写下表中的字段。 保存后点击「测试连接」和「拉取模型」。 字段 字段说明 类型调用协议。下拉里列出服务端支持的类型，常见是 OpenAI 兼容协议（DeepSeek、通义、Kimi、vLLM 等都按这个接）。 名称只用来区分不同配置，随便起，例如「DeepSeek 主账号」。必填。 Base URL厂商的接口地址，按其文档填写，例如 https://api.deepseek.com。必填。 API Key厂商给的密钥。编辑已有配置时留空表示不修改。必填。 模型列表可用的模型名，逗号分隔；手动填，或点「拉取模型」自动获取。 当前模型从模型列表里单选一个，实际调用就用它。 启用关闭后不参与翻译调用。默认模型不能关闭，要先取消默认。 设为默认翻译没有指定模型时优先用它。只有一条配置时不能取消默认。 测试连接与拉取模型 测试连接：用填好的地址和密钥发一次请求，确认能用；同时会探测这个模型支持哪些能力（工具调用、推理、JSON 输出），结果显示在提示里，比如✅ 连接成功（工具✓ 推理✓ JSON✓）。 拉取模型：向服务端索取该密钥可用的模型列表，自动填进「模型列表」，省去手写模型名。 两项都要在配置保存之后才能用。 修改与删除 点卡片上的编辑图标可以改配置；API Key 留空表示保持不变。 删除前会确认。删掉最后一条配置后，AI 翻译与 AI 对话将没有可用模型。 取消某条的「默认」时，如果还有其它配置，会自动把另一条设为默认。 和翻译、AI 对话的关系 这里配置的模型是共用的：AI 翻译和 AI 对话用的是同一条配置。换模型后，两边同时生效。 关于密钥 密钥保存在你的账号下，服务端加密存储。 界面上不会回显完整密钥，只显示是否已保存，所以编辑时无法查看原 Key，只能重新填一次。 换电脑或换浏览器后，配置仍然在账号里，不需要重新填。 相关页面 配额与用量 三种翻译排版 基于本书提问"},{"lang":"zh","path":"shelf/source-client-dir","title":"客户目录","headings":["客户目录","前提","导入","打开/解析客户目录书籍","授权只在这台电脑有效","数量限制","相关页面"],"text":"客户目录 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 客户目录 客户目录让你直接把本机某个文件夹里的电子书导入书架，不用先上传到别处。 前提 用 Chrome 或 Edge 86 及以上版本（要用浏览器的目录访问能力）。 导入时浏览器会问是否允许访问该文件夹，必须点允许。 导入 点左侧工具栏的「来源管理」，在右侧面板找到「客户目录」分区。 输入一个目录名称，它会显示在书架里。 点「导入」，在弹出的选择框里选中那个文件夹。 浏览器会弹出授权弹窗，选择「允许此网站查看和复制文件」来授权，只有允许访问后才开始扫描，支持的电子书会按原来的目录结构进入书架。 打开/解析客户目录书籍 打开前会先从本机上传到服务器并解析。 因此，只有存有这些书的电脑才能上传或加载它们。当书籍在服务器解析后，其他设备才可以正常阅读。 如果原来的授权丢失或失效（例如清除了浏览器缓存或更换了设备），需要在来源管理里重新导入该目录。 授权只在这台电脑有效 浏览器的目录授权只对这台电脑的这个浏览器有效，换个设备看不到原来的文件夹。 清过缓存、换过电脑或浏览器后，如果提示授权丢失或失效：在来源管理里点该目录的「重新导入」，重新选中同一个文件夹并允许访问。 重新导入不会重复建书，已有的书和书签都还在。 数量限制 单次导入的书籍数量、以及账号能保存的远程书籍总数，都受账号档位限制；超出时会在写入之前提示。 相关页面 来源管理 上传书籍"},{"lang":"zh","path":"shelf/source-s3","title":"S3 存储来源","headings":["S3 存储来源","添加","字段","和 WebDAV 的差别","地址限制","相关页面"],"text":"S3 存储来源 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 S3 存储来源 S3 兼容的对象存储（自建 MinIO、cloudflare R2 Object Storage、各类云厂商的对象存储）可以接入，把桶里的电子书同步到书架。 添加 点左侧工具栏的「来源管理」，在右侧面板的「网络存储」分区点「+ 添加」。 协议类型选 S3 Remote。 填下面的字段。 点「测试连接」，通过后保存并开始第一次同步。 字段 字段说明 Name显示名称，同步后在目录树中作为根节点。必填。 Endpoint存储服务地址，例如 https://s3.example.com。必填。 Bucket桶名。必填。 Prefix只扫描这个前缀下的文件，作用相当于 WebDAV 的根路径，例如 books/。留空扫描整个桶。 Region区域，默认 us-east-1。 Access Key必填。 Secret Key必填；编辑已有来源时留空表示不修改。 和 WebDAV 的差别 WebDAV 用「地址 + 根路径」定位目录；S3 用「Endpoint + Bucket + Prefix」。 其余的测试连接、同步、清理远端已删除的书、书签笔记保留，规则完全一样。 地址限制 Endpoint 只接受 http / https，且必须能从公网访问。 局域网或内网地址默认被拒绝，需要管理员在服务端加入白名单。 相关页面 来源管理 WebDAV 来源"},{"lang":"zh","path":"shelf/source-webdav","title":"WebDAV 来源","headings":["WebDAV 来源","添加","字段","同步做了什么","地址限制","数量限制","相关页面"],"text":"WebDAV 来源 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 WebDAV 来源 NAS、Nextcloud、坚果云、群晖这类支持 WebDAV 的存储，可以在这里接入，把里面的电子书同步到书架。 添加 点左侧工具栏的「来源管理」，在右侧面板的「网络存储」分区点「+ 添加」。 协议类型选 WebDAV。 填下面的字段。 点「测试连接」，通过后保存。 保存后开始第一次同步；以后可随时在卡片上点「同步」。 字段 字段说明 名称显示名称，同步后作为目录树里的根节点。 地址WebDAV 服务地址，例如 https://example.com/dav/。必填。 根路径只扫描这个子目录；留空扫描整个服务。 用户名必填。 密码必填；编辑已有来源时留空表示不修改。 超时单位秒，默认 30。 验证 SSL 证书内网自签证书时取消勾选。 同步做了什么 增量同步：只补新增、更新变化的文件，不会清空已有内容。 远程已经删掉的书，会从书架移除。 每本书的身份由「来源 + 路径」决定，路径不变则书签、笔记和阅读进度都保留。 卡片上会显示同步状态、上次同步时间和本次同步了多少本；失败时给出原因。 地址限制 只接受 http / https 地址，而且必须能从公网访问。 局域网地址（如 192.168.x.x）默认被拒绝，需要管理员在服务端加入白名单。 地址填错时保存或同步会提示「无效的连接地址」。 数量限制 单次同步的书籍数量、以及账号能保存的远程书籍总数，都受账号档位限制；超出时会在写入任何数据之前就提示。 相关页面 来源管理 S3 存储来源"},{"lang":"zh","path":"shelf/sources","title":"来源管理","headings":["来源管理","在哪里","四个分区","该用哪一种","共同点","相关页面"],"text":"来源管理 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 来源管理 来源管理决定书架里的书从哪里来：服务器上的目录、你这台电脑上的目录，或者网络存储。 在哪里 打开书架。 在左侧工具栏点「来源管理」。 右侧面板会打开「来源管理」，下面按分区列出可用的来源；再点一次左侧的按钮可以关掉。 四个分区 分区装的是什么 上传目录网站接收上传文件的目录，由管理员设置。 服务器目录网站所在服务器上的一个目录，由管理员添加。 客户目录你这台电脑上的一个文件夹，导入后书会进书架。 网络存储WebDAV 或 S3 存储里的目录，同步进书架。 分区按账号权限显示：没有权限的分区不出现。 该用哪一种 书在本机文件夹里 —— 用客户目录。 书在 NAS、网盘或对象存储里 —— 用WebDAV 或 S3。 书已经放在服务器目录里 —— 用服务器目录（管理员操作）。 共同点 客户目录导入后、网络存储同步后，书都按原来的目录结构出现在书架的目录树里。 重新导入、刷新、同步只更新文件清单，不会覆盖你手动改过的书名、作者、收藏等。 删除网络存储来源会连同它同步来的书籍一起删除，删之前先确认这些书不再需要。 客户目录、网络存储的书籍，只有在它们被打开时或批量解析时，才会从客户目录上传和从网络存储读取。并且服务器上只保存解析结果。 相关页面 客户目录 WebDAV 来源 S3 存储来源 上传书籍"},{"lang":"zh","path":"shelf/upload","title":"上传书籍","headings":["上传书籍","支持的格式","上传步骤","大小与数量限制","上传之后","相关页面"],"text":"上传书籍 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 上传书籍 可以把本地电子书上传到自己的书库。上传的书只有自己可见。 支持的格式 EPUB、MOBI、AZW3、PDF、TXT。 上传步骤 在书架顶栏点「上传书籍」。 选择本地文件，可以一次选多个。 确认后开始上传，对话框会显示进度。 上传完成后，书会出现在书架里。 大小与数量限制 单个文件的大小、一次批量上传的数量都有上限，具体数值取决于你的账号档位。超过上限时会在上传前直接提示。 上传之后 可以在书籍详情里修改书名、作者等基本信息。 可以给它加上分类和标签，方便以后在书架里筛选。 可以删除自己上传的书籍。注意，删除书籍后，所有相关的书签、笔记和阅读进度都会被清除。 相关页面 书架与视图 目录、分类与标签"},{"lang":"zh","path":"shelf/views","title":"书架与视图","headings":["书架与视图","网格与列表","排序","搜索与分页","批量操作","其它入口","相关页面"],"text":"书架与视图 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 书架与视图 书架可以换显示方式、换排序、按条件筛选，也可以批量处理多本书。 网格与列表 网格：显示封面，适合找书。 列表：每行一本，能同时看到更多信息，适合整理书库。 左侧工具栏的视图按钮在两种方式之间切换（按钮上显示当前方式）。 排序 顶栏「排序」下拉提供：最近添加、最近更新、书名 A→Z、书名 Z→A、按作者、文件大小、最近阅读。 搜索与分页 搜索框输入书名或作者，回车后筛选结果。 底部分页条切换页码；每页显示的书数固定。 批量操作 点左侧工具栏的「批量」进入多选，选中若干本后可统一处理（如删除、加入分类或标签）。 其它入口 统计：查看自己的阅读数据。 历史：最近读过的书。 设置：书架相关的选项。 左侧目录树的折叠与展开按钮，可收起导航以获得更宽的显示区域。 相关页面 目录、分类与标签 上传书籍"},{"lang":"zh","path":"start/first-book","title":"找到第一本书","headings":["找到第一本书","三种查找方式","打开一本书","书从哪里来","相关页面"],"text":"找到第一本书 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 找到第一本书 书架（站点首页）就是你的书库。公共书和自己的书都在这里。 三种查找方式 直接翻：书架默认按网格显示封面，用底部分页翻页。 按目录筛选：左侧目录树提供来源、分类、标签三类入口，点一项就只看这一类书。 搜索：顶栏搜索框输入书名或作者。 打开一本书 点击书籍封面或列表中的书名。 进入阅读器后，内容会自动按你上次的阅读设置排版。 阅读位置会自动记住，下次打开直接回到原处。 书从哪里来 公共书库：站点提供的demo书籍。 自己的书：只有自己可见。可以上传本机文件，也可以用来源管理接入客户目录或网络存储。 相关页面 书架与视图 目录、分类与标签 来源管理 上传书籍 阅读界面速览"},{"lang":"zh","path":"start/reader-tour","title":"阅读界面速览","headings":["阅读界面速览","左侧工具栏","快捷工具条","正文区","右侧面板","选中文字之后","相关页面"],"text":"阅读界面速览 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 阅读界面速览 阅读器分四块：左侧工具栏、正文区、右侧面板，一条浮在正文上方的快捷工具条。 左侧工具栏 最左边一列竖排按钮，打开面板、切换阅读模式都从这里开始。再点一次同一个按钮会收起对应的面板。 按钮作用 书架回到书架 挑一本书从书架上换一本书 显示/隐藏目录显示或隐藏章节目录 书签打开书签面板 搜索在本书内搜索文字 设置打开阅读设置面板 单页模式 / 双页模式 / 连续模式 / 单章连续模式切换阅读模式 显示书籍元数据查看这本书的信息 AI 对话打开基于本书的 AI 问答 快捷工具条 浮在正文上方的一条工具栏，管的是「怎么显示」： 明暗主题、字体、字号、行距、文字颜色、背景色，以及「重置外观」。 宽度与「推荐」；分页模式下还有顶部留白、底部留白。 加书签、开始翻译。 右上角的箭头可以隐藏或重新显示这一条。 正文区 连续模式下上下滚动；分页模式下左右翻页。翻到一章的开头或结尾时，可以继续翻到下一章。 右侧面板 目录、书签、搜索、设置、AI 对话、书籍信息都从右侧滑出，同一时间只显示一个。 选中文字之后 在正文里选中文字会弹出操作菜单：拷贝、笔记、书签、马克笔、直线、波浪线、搜索、翻译、AI，以及五种颜色。详见 笔记与标注。 相关页面 四种阅读模式 阅读设置总览"},{"lang":"zh","path":"start/sign-in","title":"注册与登录","headings":["注册与登录","注册","登录方式","忘记密码","登录状态","相关页面"],"text":"注册与登录 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 注册与登录 不注册也可以使用。系统会自动保留你的数据。需要更多功能时再注册账号，注册账号时，你以前的浏览、阅读、进度、书签和笔记都会跟着账号走。 注册 点页面左下角的「登录」。 在登录页切换到「注册」。 填写邮箱与密码，提交后即可使用。 登录方式 用户名 + 密码。 第三方账号：登录页下方会显示本站已开启的第三方登录入口（如 Google、Apple、Twitter、LINE、Kakao、Yandex）。点击后按提示授权即可。 忘记密码 在登录页点「忘记密码」。 填写注册时的邮箱，提交后会收到重置邮件。 按邮件里的链接设置新密码。 登录状态 关闭浏览器再打开，通常会保持登录。 如果提示登录已过期，重新登录即可；阅读进度和书签不会丢失。 相关页面 找到第一本书 个人资料与密码"},{"lang":"zh","path":"start/what-is","title":"认识 FacetShelf","headings":["认识 FacetShelf","三大能力","你需要准备什么","下一步"],"text":"认识 FacetShelf · FacetShelf 帮助中心 认识 FacetShelf FacetShelf 是一个在浏览器里使用的多语言阅读平台。打开网页就能读书，不需要安装任何软件。 三大能力 电子书阅读器：支持 EPUB、MOBI、AZW3、PDF、TXT 格式；可以上传自己的书籍，也可以读取本机文件夹（客户目录）和网络存储（WebDAV 或 S3）。 多语言阅读平台：把一本书翻译成另一种语言，支持行间对照、仅看译文和双列对照三种版式。 AI 辅助阅读：基于这本书的内容回答问题，回答里的引用可以直接跳回原文核对。 你需要准备什么 一个现代浏览器（建议使用电脑浏览器，以获得双列对照等完整排版）。 不需要注册也能浏览和阅读；注册后可以使用更多的功能。 系统会提供少量 token 用于试用 AI 翻译与 AI 对话；也可以填入自己的大模型 API Key（BYOK）。 下一步 注册与登录 —— 账号、第三方登录与匿名使用 找到第一本书 —— 浏览书库、筛选与搜索 四种阅读模式 —— 选一种适合你的阅读方式"},{"lang":"zh","path":"translation/modes","title":"三种翻译排版","headings":["三种翻译排版","行间对照","仅译文","双列对照","译文主题","相关页面"],"text":"三种翻译排版 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 三种翻译排版 AI 翻译有三种显示方式，在阅读设置的「AI 翻译」分区里切换。 行间对照 每一段原文后面紧跟它的译文，原文和译文在同一栏里上下排列。 适合逐句核对，或想边看原文边看译文。 篇幅会比原文长。 仅译文 只显示译文，原文不再显示。 适合只想读译文的情况。 需要核对原文时，切回行间对照即可。 双列对照 原文和译文左右并排，两列同步滚动。 适合大屏幕。 「双列总宽度」可以调整两列合起来的总宽度，每列各占一半。 译文主题 译文部分可以套用不同的视觉主题（默认、羊皮纸、细边框），用来和原文区分开。 相关页面 翻译范围与语言 划词翻译"},{"lang":"zh","path":"translation/scope-language","title":"翻译范围与语言","headings":["翻译范围与语言","三种范围","源语言与目标语言","开始翻译","相关页面"],"text":"翻译范围与语言 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 翻译范围与语言 先决定翻译多少内容，再决定翻译成什么语言。 三种范围 范围行为适合 跟随阅读读到哪译到哪只想看一部分，或不想一次等太久 当前章把当前这一章整体翻译要连续读这一章 整书把整本书都翻译准备从头读到尾 范围越大，一次等待的时间越长，消耗也越多；可以先小范围看看效果。 源语言与目标语言 源语言：书原本的语言，通常会自动识别。 目标语言：要翻译成的语言，必须与源语言不同。 开始翻译 打开一本书，在「AI 翻译」分区里设置模式、范围与目标语言。 点快捷工具条上的「开始翻译」。 在右侧面板「翻译控制台」中可以查看翻译进度。 翻译过程中可以继续阅读；已译好的部分会立即显示。 相关页面 三种翻译排版 配额与用量"},{"lang":"zh","path":"translation/selection","title":"划词翻译","headings":["划词翻译","怎么用","字数上限","与整书翻译的区别","相关页面"],"text":"划词翻译 · FacetShelf 帮助中心 划词翻译 只想弄懂一句话或一段话时，不用开启整书翻译。 怎么用 在正文里选中要翻译的文字。 在弹出菜单里点「翻译」。 译文会立刻显示出来。 字数上限 一次最多翻译 4000 个字符。超出时会在本地直接提示，不会发起请求；需要更长的话请分次选中，或改用整章翻译。 与整书翻译的区别 划词翻译整书翻译 范围你选中的那一段跟随阅读 / 当前章 / 整书 是否保留临时结果，不写进书里译好后随书显示 适合查一句话、看生词整段、整章、整本地读 相关页面 三种翻译排版 笔记与标注"},{"lang":"en","path":"account/language","title":"Interface Language","headings":["Interface Language","Available languages","Switching","Three things not to confuse","Related pages"],"text":"Interface Language · FacetShelf Help Center Interface Language The interface language only changes the site's own wording — buttons, menus and messages. It never changes what is inside a book. Available languages 简体中文, 繁體中文, English, 日本語, 한국어, Deutsch, Español, Français. Switching Use the Language dropdown at the top of the side panel — in the reader and on the Shelf. The sign-in page and the landing page have a language picker too. The interface switches immediately. Your choice survives a page refresh. Three things not to confuse ConceptWhat it affects Interface languageSite wording: buttons, menus, messages The book's languageThe content of the book; the interface language never changes it Translation target languageThe language AI Translation turns a book into Related pages Reading Settings Overview Translation Scope & Languages"},{"lang":"en","path":"account/profile","title":"Profile & Password","headings":["Profile & Password","Update your details","Change your password","When the login state goes wrong","Related pages"],"text":"Profile & Password · FacetShelf Help Center Profile & Password Everything account-related lives on the profile page. Update your details Log in and open your profile. Edit your email, display name and other basics. Changes take effect as soon as you save. Change your password Find the password area on the profile page. Enter your current password and a new one, then submit. You are asked to log in again with the new password. If you have forgotten the current password, use Forgot password? on the sign-in page. When the login state goes wrong After a long time away you may be told the session expired; log in again. Reading position, bookmarks and notes are stored with the account and are still there after logging back in. If the browser blocks cookies, the login state may not persist. Related pages Sign In Interface Language Troubleshooting"},{"lang":"en","path":"ai/chat","title":"Ask About This Book","headings":["Ask About This Book","Open the chat","What to ask","Where the answer comes from","How to use them","What the two marks mean","Why there is sometimes an outline but no highlight","Related pages"],"text":"Ask About This Book · FacetShelf Help Center Ask About This Book The AI first looks for relevant passages in the book you are reading, then answers from them — rather than talking in generalities from outside knowledge. Open the chat Open a book. Click AI Chat in the toolbar; the chat panel opens on the right. Type a question and send it. What to ask Summarize — \"What is this chapter mainly about?\" Explain — \"What does X mean here?\" Locate — \"Where is Y first mentioned in the book?\" Compare — \"How does the author's view of A differ from B?\" Follow up — keep asking about the previous answer; you do not need to repeat the context. Where the answer comes from The numbered markers in an answer are citations. Every answer shows which passage of the book it is based on, and you can click through to check it yourself. How to use them Ask a question in AI Chat and wait for the answer to finish. Click any numbered marker. The reader jumps to the matching chapter and passage, and marks the cited spot. What the two marks mean MarkMeaning Yellow outline The paragraph the answer cites — \"the source is here\". Yellow highlight The exact sentences from the original that the answer actually uses word for word — \"these are the lines\". Why there is sometimes an outline but no highlight If the AI summarizes or paraphrases a paragraph, no sentence from the original is used intact, so only the paragraph is outlined. That tells you the answer relies on the meaning of the paragraph rather than on one particular sentence. Related pages Chat Sessions Quota & Usage"},{"lang":"en","path":"ai/quota","title":"Quota & Usage","headings":["Quota & Usage","How usage is counted","When the quota runs out","Using less","Related pages"],"text":"Quota & Usage · FacetShelf Help Center Quota & Usage A small token allowance is included for trying AI Translation and AI Chat; you can also plug in your own model API key (BYOK). How usage is counted Both translation and chat use the allowance; how much depends on the amount of text processed. Whole book > current chapter > translate while reading — the larger the range, the more it uses. Ordinary reading, bookmarks, notes and search use none. When the quota runs out A new AI request shows a message that this month's quota is used up. Content already translated and conversations already finished are unaffected and stay readable. The simplest fix is to use your own API key (BYOK). Using less Try Translate while reading on a few passages to judge quality before committing to the whole book. To understand a single sentence, use Translate Selection — far cheaper than a chapter. Do not repeat the same question; add to the previous answer instead. Related pages Translation Scope & Languages Ask About This Book"},{"lang":"en","path":"ai/sessions","title":"Chat Sessions","headings":["Chat Sessions","New chat","History","Tips","Related pages"],"text":"Chat Sessions · FacetShelf Help Center Chat Sessions A run of related questions about one book belongs to a single session. Start a new one when you change topic — the answers stay more focused. New chat Click New chat in the chat panel; everything you ask from then on belongs to that session. History The panel lists this book's earlier sessions, newest first. Click any one to switch to it and continue that conversation. Times are shown relative to now: Just now, N min ago, N h ago, N d ago. Tips Keep one session to one topic; answers are more accurate. Sessions are kept per book, so opening another book does not mix them up. Related pages Ask About This Book Quota & Usage"},{"lang":"en","path":"faq/index","title":"FAQ","headings":["FAQ","General","Do I need an account?","Where is my data stored?","Which browsers are supported?","Do I need my own AI API key?","Books and formats","Which formats are supported?","Can I read DRM-protected books?","Why does PDF not look ideal?","Are there upload limits?","AI features","How long does translation take?","Why does a citation have an outline but no highlight?","What if my AI quota runs out?","Still stuck?"],"text":"FAQ · FacetShelf Help Center FAQ General Do I need an account? No. The site works without one, and your reading position, bookmarks and notes are kept as you go. Where is my data stored? FacetShelf is an online service. Library entries, reading positions, bookmarks, notes and AI conversations are stored on the site's servers, not locally. Books you upload privately are visible only to you. Which browsers are supported? A recent version of Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari. Layouts such as dual-column bilingual look best on a desktop browser. Do I need my own AI API key? A small token allowance is included for trying AI Translation and AI Chat; you can also plug in your own model API key (BYOK). Books and formats Which formats are supported? EPUB, MOBI, AZW3, PDF and TXT. Can I read DRM-protected books? No. Books with DRM cannot be parsed. Why does PDF not look ideal? PDF is a fixed layout, which is hard to re-parse. For now a PDF is shown in its original layout; streaming reflow for PDF is planned. Are there upload limits? Yes. The size of a single file and the number of files in one batch depend on your plan; you are warned before uploading. AI features How long does translation take? It depends on the range: translate while reading is nearly immediate, a chapter takes a little while, a whole book takes longest. You can keep reading while it runs — translated parts appear first. Why does a citation have an outline but no highlight? It means the AI used the meaning of that paragraph — summarizing or paraphrasing it — so no sentence from the original is used word for word. See Ask About This Book. What if my AI quota runs out? New AI requests report that the monthly quota is used up. Reading, bookmarks and notes are unaffected, and translated content already generated stays readable. See Quota & Usage. Still stuck? Try Troubleshooting, or use Contact in the site footer."},{"lang":"en","path":"faq/troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting","headings":["Troubleshooting","A book will not open","No translation appears","The AI does not respond","I keep getting logged out","A page still shows old content","Still not solved"],"text":"Troubleshooting · FacetShelf Help Center Troubleshooting A book will not open Refresh the page and try once more. Check that the book is EPUB, PDF, MOBI, AZW3 or TXT. If it was just uploaded, wait for the upload to finish before opening it. Large files take longer the first time they are opened. No translation appears Check that a translation mode other than Off is selected in the AI Translation section. Check that the target language differs from the book's language. Translate while reading only translates where you are reading; go back to a translated part to see it. Check whether a quota warning is shown. The AI does not respond Check whether it says the quota is used up. Wait a moment and try again, or ask a shorter question. If nothing happens for a long time, refresh the page and ask again. I keep getting logged out Just log in again; your reading data is not lost. If it keeps happening, check whether the browser blocks cookies or is in private mode. Signing the same account in from several places in quick succession can produce a session-expired message. A page still shows old content Press Ctrl + F5 to force a refresh that bypasses the browser cache. Still not solved Use Contact in the site footer and tell us: which book, on which page, what you did, and what message you saw."},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/annotations","title":"Notes & Annotations","headings":["Notes & Annotations","What the menu offers","Five colors","Notes","Turning the popup off","Related pages"],"text":"Notes & Annotations · FacetShelf Help Center Notes & Annotations Select text in the book and a menu appears. What the menu offers ActionWhat it does CopyCopies the selected text NoteAdds a note to the selected text BookmarkBookmarks this passage HighlighterPuts a colored background behind the text Underline / WavyDraws a line under the text SearchSearches the book for the selected text TranslateTranslates the selected text AIAsks the AI about the selected text Five colors A row of colors sits below the menu: Red, Purple, Blue, Green and Gold. Which one new annotations use by default is set in the Bookmarks & Annotations section of reading settings. Notes Select text, click Note, write in the box and save. Notes can be reviewed in the bookmarks panel; how a note previews (Hover or Click) is set in reading settings. An existing note can be reopened, edited or deleted. Turning the popup off If you would rather not see the menu on every selection, set Selection Popup to Context Menu (right click) or Off. Related pages Bookmarks Reading Settings Overview Translate Selection"},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/appearance","title":"Appearance & Theme","headings":["Appearance & Theme","Font and size","Color and background","Custom CSS","Light and dark theme","Related pages"],"text":"Appearance & Theme · FacetShelf Help Center Appearance & Theme Appearance only changes how the book looks; the content and the book file stay untouched. Font and size Font — pick a built-in font or Book Default. When a local font is used, the browser may ask for permission. Font Size — enlarges or shrinks the text as a whole. Line Spacing / Letter Spacing / Para Margin — control the space between lines, between letters, and between paragraphs. Color and background Text Color — hexadecimal (e.g. #333333) or rgb(...). Background Color — #rrggbb or rgba(...); leave empty to follow the book. Background Image — a CSS background image URL. Empty values follow the book instead of overriding it. Custom CSS If you know CSS, you can refine the text further — for example a first-line indent: p { text-indent: 2em; } If not, just leave it empty. Light and dark theme The quick controls bar has a light/dark toggle; it switches the theme of the reader interface. It is separate from the background color above: the theme styles the interface, the background color styles the text. Related pages Reading Settings Overview Reading Profiles"},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/bookmarks","title":"Bookmarks","headings":["Bookmarks","Add a bookmark","Review and jump","Sorting and paging","How bookmarks differ from notes"],"text":"Bookmarks · FacetShelf Help Center Bookmarks A bookmark records a position, so you can jump straight back and carry on. Add a bookmark Go to the place you want to remember. Click Bookmark on the quick controls bar above the text. The current page (or position, in continuous modes) is recorded. Review and jump Click Bookmarks in the left toolbar to open the panel. The panel lists every bookmark in this book. Click any one and the text jumps there. Sorting and paging Bookmarks can be sorted by time or by position, using the two sort buttons in the panel (Sort by time / Sort by position). Many bookmarks are shown page by page; how many per page is set in the Panel Settings section of reading settings. How bookmarks differ from notes A bookmark records a position only. To mark a passage or write a note, use Notes & Annotations."},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/modes","title":"Reading Modes","headings":["Reading Modes","The four modes","How to switch","Related pages"],"text":"Reading Modes · FacetShelf Help Center Reading Modes The reader offers four layouts. They only change how pages are arranged — never the content of the book. The four modes ModeHow it looksGood for Continuous Scrolls through the whole book, showing several chapters at once Long sessions, and readers who prefer scrolling up and down Single Frame One chapter at a time, scrolling inside that chapter Working through chapter by chapter without left-right paging Single Page One page at a time, turned left and right A paper-like page-turning feel Double Page Two pages side by side Large screens, or seeing what comes before and after How to switch Open any book to enter the reader. Click Single Page, Double Page, Continuous or Single Frame in the left toolbar. The Layout section of reading settings has finer options, such as whether to move into the next chapter automatically at a boundary. When you switch modes, the reader tries to keep your place. Converting between paged and scrolling layouts can land you a page away from where you were. Related pages Paging & Position Reading Settings Overview Appearance & Theme"},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/navigate","title":"Paging & Position","headings":["Paging & Position","Turning pages","Moving between chapters","Resuming where you left off","Width and margins","Related pages"],"text":"Paging & Position · FacetShelf Help Center Paging & Position Two ways to move: scroll in continuous modes, turn pages in paged modes. At the edge of a chapter you carry on into the next one. Turning pages Paged modes: click the left or right half of the text area; the arrow keys, PageUp / PageDown and Space (Shift+Space goes back) also work. Continuous modes: just scroll up and down. Moving between chapters Keep going past the end of a chapter to enter the next one; go back past the start to enter the previous one. Boundary Nav can be Auto or Manual: with Auto, reaching a boundary and continuing moves you on; with Manual you have to ask for it. When you go back into the previous chapter, Previous Landing decides whether you land at its start or its end. Resuming where you left off Opening a book returns to the place you last read. To always start at the first page, turn off Restore Position in the Reading Behavior section of reading settings. Width and margins Width on the quick controls bar changes the width of the text; Fit returns to the recommended proportion. In paged modes you can also set the top and bottom margins separately. Related pages Reading Modes Reading Settings Overview"},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/offline","title":"Offline Reading","headings":["Offline Reading","Turn it on","Download the whole book","While offline","What does not work offline","Cache and cleanup","Related pages"],"text":"Offline Reading · FacetShelf Help Center Offline Reading Offline Reading exists so you can keep reading when the network is gone. Turn it on in Settings. Chapters you read from then on are cached automatically; you can also download the whole book at once to cache every chapter. Turn it on Open Settings in the reader toolbar (each section is described in Reading Settings Overview). Expand the Reading Behavior section. Set Offline Reading to On. It is off by default. Once it is on, a Download Offline button appears in the bottom-right corner of the reader. Turn it off and the button disappears; cached pages are no longer served. Download the whole book Click Download Offline in the bottom-right corner to cache the whole book: every chapter, the contents, the cover and the book info. A progress bar shows while it runs; on completion you briefly see Offline ✓, then the button returns. Click it again whenever you want to refresh the cache. You can read offline without downloading, but only chapters you have opened on this device are cached. One click on Download Offline fills in the rest of the book. While offline An Offline Mode badge appears in the bottom-right corner. Books you have downloaded open as usual — you can move between chapters and jump through the contents. For a book you have not downloaded, or a chapter that is not cached yet, a message says the chapter is not cached; come back when you are online. What does not work offline Features that need a network: AI Translation, AI Chat, selection translation and the like. Offline you read the original text; translations have to be generated online. Cache and cleanup Downloaded content lives in the browser on this device; another device has to download it again. The cache is not tied to an account: logging in, logging out, switching accounts, or a session expiring clears the downloaded books on this device, and they have to be downloaded again. There is no Clear cache button in the app. Setting Offline Reading to off only stops the cache from being served — downloaded content stays in the browser. To remove it completely, use the browser's Clear site data. Related pages Reading Settings Overview Paging & Position Troubleshooting"},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/profiles","title":"Reading Profiles","headings":["Reading Profiles","The default profile","Save As","Switching and deleting","Typical uses","Related pages"],"text":"Reading Profiles · FacetShelf Help Center Reading Profiles A complete set of reading settings is one profile. Keep several for different situations and switch whenever you like. The default profile Every change is saved automatically into a profile named default. default cannot be deleted. Save As Adjust the settings you want. In the Reader Configuration section, enter a name and click Save As. Those settings become a separate profile. If the name already exists, you are asked whether to overwrite it. Switching and deleting Pick a profile from the dropdown and its settings apply immediately. Deleting a profile asks for confirmation; it cannot be undone. To change a saved profile: select it, adjust the settings, then save it again under the same name. Typical uses One for daytime reading (light background, larger text) and one for night (dark, wider line spacing). One with the width you like for dual-column bilingual translation. Related pages Reading Settings Overview Appearance & Theme"},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/settings","title":"Reading Settings Overview","headings":["Reading Settings Overview","The eight sections","Saving and restoring","Related pages"],"text":"Reading Settings Overview · FacetShelf Help Center Reading Settings Overview Click Settings in the toolbar to open the panel. Changes apply at once and are saved automatically. The eight sections SectionWhat it controls Reader ConfigurationChoosing, saving and deleting profiles LayoutWidth for each mode, and top and bottom margins in paged modes AppearanceFont, font size, colors, background, line spacing, letter spacing, paragraph margin, custom CSS Reading BehaviorTheme, reading mode, restore position, boundary navigation, page animation, Offline Reading, selection popup Bookmarks & AnnotationsDefault color for new annotations, and how note previews appear Panel SettingsHow many bookmarks and search results fit on a page AI TranslationTranslation mode, range, translation theme, source and target language AI ModelThe AI service shared by AI Translation and AI Chat Saving and restoring Every change is saved to the current profile immediately; there is no Save button. Changes only affect the reader — the book's file is never modified. To keep several setups, use Reading Profiles. Related pages Appearance & Theme Paging & Position Translation Layouts"},{"lang":"en","path":"reading/toc-search","title":"Contents & In-Book Search","headings":["Contents & In-Book Search","Contents","Search inside the book","Paging through results","Related pages"],"text":"Contents & In-Book Search · FacetShelf Help Center Contents & In-Book Search Contents is for jumping between chapters; search is for finding one particular sentence. Contents Click TOC in the toolbar; the chapter list opens on the right. Click any chapter and the text jumps to its beginning. Click TOC again to close the panel. Search inside the book Click Search in the toolbar, type keywords and press Enter. You can enter several keywords separated by spaces; they are combined with AND. Results are listed by chapter and show the matching snippets. Click a result to jump there; the matching text is highlighted. Paging through results Many results are shown page by page. How many fit on a page is set in the Panel Settings section of reading settings; by default it adapts to the panel height. Related pages Bookmarks Reading Settings Overview"},{"lang":"en","path":"shelf/facets","title":"Contents, Categories & Tags","headings":["Contents, Categories & Tags","Three entries","Filtering","Searching within a filter","Related pages"],"text":"Contents, Categories & Tags · FacetShelf Help Center Contents, Categories & Tags The contents tree on the left gives you three ways to narrow the library down to what you are looking for. Three entries EntryWhat it means SourcesWhich library or folder a book comes from CategoriesGrouped by topic, maintained by the site or by you TagsFree-form keywords; a book can have several Filtering Expand the contents tree and click a category or tag. The Shelf shows only books in that group; the top bar shows the current filter and the number of books. To clear the filter, click the × next to it in the top bar, or go back to All. Searching within a filter With a category or tag selected, the search box looks only inside that group. Related pages Shelf & Views Uploading Books"},{"lang":"en","path":"shelf/llm-provider","title":"AI Model Settings","headings":["AI Model Settings","Where to find it","Add a model","Fields","Test connection and fetch models","Edit and delete","Shared with translation and AI Chat","About the key","Related pages"],"text":"AI Model Settings · FacetShelf Help Center AI Model Settings AI Translation and AI Chat both need a large language model. Here you can plug in your own API key and call it with your own vendor account and quota. Where to find it Open the Shelf. Click Settings in the left toolbar. Find AI Model in the right-hand panel. Add a model Click + Add. Choose a Type and fill in the fields below. Save, then click Test connection and Fetch models. Fields FieldNotes TypeThe calling protocol. The dropdown lists the types the server supports; the common one is the OpenAI-compatible protocol (DeepSeek, Qwen, Kimi, vLLM and others all connect this way). NameOnly used to tell configurations apart — anything works, e.g. \"DeepSeek main account\". Required. Base URLThe vendor's API endpoint, as documented by the vendor, e.g. https://api.deepseek.com. Required. API KeyThe key issued by the vendor. When editing, leave empty to keep the current key. Required. Model list (comma-separated)Available model names, comma-separated; type them by hand or click Fetch models. Current model (single selection)Pick one from the model list; this is the model actually called. EnabledWhen disabled, the model is not used for translation. A default model cannot be disabled — unset its default first. Set as defaultUsed first when a translation does not name a model. With only one configuration, the default cannot be unset. Test connection and fetch models Test connection — sends one request with the address and key to confirm they work. It also probes which capabilities the model supports (tool calling, reasoning, JSON output) and shows the result, e.g. ✅ Connection successful (tools ✓ reasoning ✓ JSON ✓). Fetch models — asks the server for the models this key can use and fills the model list, so you do not have to type names. Both are available only after the configuration has been saved. Edit and delete Click the edit icon on a card to change the configuration; leaving API Key empty keeps it unchanged. Deleting asks for confirmation. After the last configuration is deleted, AI Translation and AI Chat have no model to use. If you unset one card as default and other configurations exist, another one automatically becomes the default. Shared with translation and AI Chat The model configured here is shared: AI Translation and AI Chat use the same configuration. Changing it takes effect in both at once. About the key The key is stored with your account and encrypted on the server. The full key is never shown again; the interface only says whether one is saved. When editing you cannot read the old key, so enter it again. On another computer or browser the configuration is still in your account; nothing needs re-entering. Related pages Quota & Usage Translation Layouts Ask About This Book"},{"lang":"en","path":"shelf/source-client-dir","title":"Client Directory","headings":["Client Directory","Requirements","Import","Opening books from a Client Directory","The permission stays on this computer","Limits","Related pages"],"text":"Client Directory · FacetShelf Help Center Client Directory A Client Directory brings e-books from a folder on this computer into the Shelf, without uploading them anywhere first. Requirements Chrome or Edge 86 or later (the browser's directory access is used). When the browser asks whether to allow access to the folder, you must allow it. Import Click Sources in the left toolbar, then find the Client Directory section. Enter a directory name; it will be shown on the Shelf. Click Import and choose the folder in the picker. The browser asks for permission — choose Allow this site to view and copy files. Scanning starts only after you allow it, and supported books join the Shelf with their original folder structure. Opening books from a Client Directory Before a book opens, it is uploaded from this computer to the server and parsed. That is why only the computer holding the files can upload or load them. Once a book has been parsed on the server, other devices can read it. If the permission is lost (for example after clearing browser data, or on another device), import the directory again from Sources. The permission stays on this computer The browser's folder permission applies to this browser on this computer only. Another device cannot see the folder. If a permission is lost or expires, click Re-import on that directory in Sources, choose the same folder and allow access. Re-importing does not create duplicates; existing books and bookmarks stay. Limits How many books a single import can add, and how many remote books an account can keep, both depend on your plan. You are warned before anything is written. Related pages Sources Uploading Books"},{"lang":"en","path":"shelf/source-s3","title":"S3 Source","headings":["S3 Source","Add a source","Fields","How S3 differs from WebDAV","Address rules","Related pages"],"text":"S3 Source · FacetShelf Help Center S3 Source S3-compatible object storage — self-hosted MinIO, Cloudflare R2, or a cloud provider's object storage — can be connected here, and the e-books in a bucket can be synced to the Shelf. Add a source Click Sources in the left toolbar, then + Add in the Network Storage section. Choose S3 Remote as the protocol. Fill in the fields below. Click Test Connection; save once it succeeds and the first sync starts. Fields FieldNotes NameDisplay name; after syncing it becomes the root node in the contents tree. Required. Endpoint URLThe storage endpoint, e.g. https://s3.example.com. Required. BucketBucket name. Required. PrefixScan only files under this prefix — the equivalent of WebDAV's Root Path, e.g. books/. Leave empty to scan the whole bucket. RegionRegion; us-east-1 by default. Access KeyRequired. Secret KeyRequired; when editing an existing source, leave empty to keep the current one. How S3 differs from WebDAV WebDAV locates a directory with Server URL + Root Path; S3 uses Endpoint URL + Bucket + Prefix. Everything else works the same: test connection, sync, removing books deleted remotely, and keeping bookmarks and notes. Address rules The endpoint must be http or https, and must be reachable from the public internet. Local and intranet addresses are rejected by default; an administrator can add them to a server-side allowlist. Related pages Sources WebDAV Source"},{"lang":"en","path":"shelf/source-webdav","title":"WebDAV Source","headings":["WebDAV Source","Add a source","Fields","What a sync does","Address rules","Limits","Related pages"],"text":"WebDAV Source · FacetShelf Help Center WebDAV Source Any storage that speaks WebDAV — a NAS, Nextcloud, Jianguoyun, Synology and the like — can be connected here, and its e-books can be synced to the Shelf. Add a source Click Sources in the left toolbar, then + Add in the Network Storage section. Choose WebDAV as the protocol. Fill in the fields below. Click Test Connection; save once it succeeds. The first sync starts right after saving. Later, click Sync on the card whenever you like. Fields FieldNotes NameDisplay name; after syncing it becomes the root node in the contents tree. Server URLThe WebDAV endpoint, e.g. https://example.com/dav/. Required. Root PathScan only this subfolder; leave empty to scan the whole server. UsernameRequired. PasswordRequired; when editing an existing source, leave empty to keep the current one. Timeout (s)In seconds; 30 by default. Verify SSL CertificateUncheck for self-signed certificates on a local network. What a sync does Incremental: it only adds new files and updates changed ones; nothing already there is cleared. Books deleted remotely are removed from the Shelf. A book is identified by its source + path. As long as the path stays the same, its bookmarks, notes and reading position are kept. The card shows the sync state, the time of the last sync and how many books were synced; failures come with a reason. Address rules Only http and https addresses are accepted, and they must be reachable from the public internet. Local addresses such as 192.168.x.x are rejected by default; an administrator can add them to a server-side allowlist. If the address is wrong, saving or syncing reports an invalid connection address. Limits How many books a single sync can add, and how many remote books an account can keep, both depend on your plan. You are warned before any data is written. Related pages Sources S3 Source"},{"lang":"en","path":"shelf/sources","title":"Sources","headings":["Sources","Where to find it","Four sections","Which one to use","What they share","Related pages"],"text":"Sources · FacetShelf Help Center Sources Sources decides where the books on your Shelf come from: a directory on the server, a folder on this computer, or network storage. Where to find it Open the Shelf. Click Sources in the left toolbar. The Sources panel opens on the right, listing the source types available to you; click the button again to close it. Four sections SectionWhat it holds Upload DirectoryThe directory where the site receives uploaded files, set by an administrator. Server DirectoryA directory on the server that hosts the site, added by an administrator. Client DirectoryA folder on this computer; once imported, its books join the Shelf. Network StorageA directory on WebDAV or S3 storage, synced into the Shelf. Which sections appear depends on your account: sections you have no access to are hidden. Which one to use Books are in a folder on this computer — use Client Directory. Books are on a NAS, cloud drive or object storage — use WebDAV or S3. Books are already on the server — use Server Directory (an administrator sets it up). What they share After an import or a sync, books appear in the contents tree with their original folder structure. Re-importing, refreshing or syncing only updates the file list; it never overwrites titles, authors or favorites you changed by hand. Deleting a network source also deletes the books it synced. Make sure you no longer need them first. Books from a Client Directory or network storage are read only when opened, or during a batch parse. The server keeps only the parsed result. Related pages Client Directory WebDAV Source S3 Source Uploading Books"},{"lang":"en","path":"shelf/upload","title":"Uploading Books","headings":["Uploading Books","Supported formats","Upload steps","Size and count limits","After uploading","Related pages"],"text":"Uploading Books · FacetShelf Help Center Uploading Books You can upload e-books from this computer to your own library. Uploaded books are visible only to you. Supported formats EPUB, MOBI, AZW3, PDF and TXT. Upload steps Click Upload in the Shelf top bar. Choose files from this computer; you can pick several at once. Confirm and the upload starts; the dialog shows progress. When it finishes, the books appear on the Shelf. Size and count limits There is an upper limit on each file and on how many files one batch can contain; the exact numbers depend on your plan. You are warned before the upload starts. After uploading You can edit the title, author and other basics in the book details. You can add categories and tags, so the book is easy to filter later. You can delete books you uploaded. Deleting a book also clears its bookmarks, notes and reading position. Related pages Shelf & Views Contents, Categories & Tags"},{"lang":"en","path":"shelf/views","title":"Shelf & Views","headings":["Shelf & Views","Grid and list","Sorting","Search and paging","Batch actions","Other entries","Related pages"],"text":"Shelf & Views · FacetShelf Help Center Shelf & Views The Shelf can change how books are shown, how they are sorted, which ones are listed — and it can act on several books at once. Grid and list Grid — covers only, good for browsing. List — one book per row, with more details at once; good for organizing. The view button in the left toolbar switches between them; the button shows the current view. Sorting The Sort by dropdown in the top bar offers: Recently Added, Recently Updated, Title A→Z, Title Z→A, By Author, File Size and Recently Read. Search and paging Type a title or author in the search box and press Enter. The pager at the bottom switches pages. How many books fit on a page follows your Shelf settings. Batch actions Click Batch in the left toolbar to select several books, then remove them, add them to a category, or add tags. Other entries My Stats — your reading statistics. History — books you read recently. Settings — options for the Shelf. The collapse and expand control on the contents tree gives the grid more room. Related pages Contents, Categories & Tags Uploading Books"},{"lang":"en","path":"start/first-book","title":"Find Your First Book","headings":["Find Your First Book","Three ways to find a book","Open a book","Where books come from","Related pages"],"text":"Find Your First Book · FacetShelf Help Center Find Your First Book The Shelf — the site home page — is your library. Public books and your own books all live here. Three ways to find a book Just browse — the Shelf shows covers in a grid by default; turn pages at the bottom. Narrow by contents — the contents tree on the left offers Sources, Categories and Tags. Pick one to show only that group. Search — type a title or author in the top bar. Open a book Click a cover, or a title in the list view. The reader opens with the reading settings you used last time. Your position is remembered, so the next visit returns to the same place. Where books come from Public library — sample books provided by the site. Your own books — only you can see them. Upload files, or connect a Client Directory or network storage through Sources. Related pages Shelf & Views Contents, Categories & Tags Sources Uploading Books Reader at a Glance"},{"lang":"en","path":"start/reader-tour","title":"Reader at a Glance","headings":["Reader at a Glance","Left toolbar","Quick controls","Text area","Side panels","After selecting text","Related pages"],"text":"Reader at a Glance · FacetShelf Help Center Reader at a Glance The reader has four parts: the toolbar on the left, the text area, the side panels, and a quick controls bar floating above the text. Left toolbar A vertical column of buttons on the far left. Opening a panel or switching reading mode starts here. Clicking the same button again closes its panel. ButtonWhat it does ShelfBack to the Shelf BookshelfOpen another book TOCShow or hide the chapter contents BookmarksOpen the bookmarks panel SearchSearch inside this book SettingsOpen reading settings Single Page / Double Page / Continuous / Single FrameSwitch reading mode Book InfoSee details about this book AI ChatAsk questions about this book Quick controls A bar floating above the text. It controls how the book looks: Theme, font, font size, line spacing, text color, background color, and Reset. Width and Fit; in paged modes, top and bottom margins as well. Bookmark and Start translating. The arrow at the right end collapses or restores the bar. Text area Scroll vertically in continuous modes; turn pages in paged modes. At the start or end of a chapter you can keep going into the next one. Side panels Contents, bookmarks, search, settings, AI Chat and book info all slide in from the right; only one is open at a time. After selecting text Selecting text opens a menu: Copy, Note, Bookmark, Highlighter, Underline, Wavy, Search, Translate and AI, plus five colors. See Notes & Annotations. Related pages Reading Modes Reading Settings Overview"},{"lang":"en","path":"start/sign-in","title":"Sign In","headings":["Sign In","Sign up","Ways to log in","Forgot password","Staying signed in","Related pages"],"text":"Sign In · FacetShelf Help Center Sign In You can use the site without an account — your data is kept on this device. Sign up when you want more; whatever you have already done here (browsing, reading position, bookmarks, notes) moves to the new account. Sign up Click Log in at the bottom left of the page. On the sign-in page, switch to Sign Up. Enter an email and a password, then submit. Ways to log in Username and password. Social account — the sign-in page lists the providers this site has enabled (such as Google, Apple, Twitter, LINE, Kakao, Yandex). Click one and follow the prompts. Forgot password On the sign-in page, click Forgot password? Enter the email you registered with; a reset email will arrive. Follow the link in the email to set a new password. Staying signed in Usually you remain signed in after closing and reopening the browser. If you see a message that the session expired, log in again. Your reading position and bookmarks are not lost. Related pages Find Your First Book Profile & Password"},{"lang":"en","path":"start/what-is","title":"What is FacetShelf","headings":["What is FacetShelf","What you can do","What you need","Next steps"],"text":"What is FacetShelf · FacetShelf Help Center What is FacetShelf FacetShelf is a multilingual reading platform that runs in your browser. Open a web page and start reading — there is nothing to install. What you can do Read almost anything — EPUB, MOBI, AZW3, PDF and TXT. Bring your own books by uploading them, reading a folder on this computer, or connecting network storage (WebDAV or S3). Read across languages — translate a book into another language and choose how the two texts are laid out: interlinear, translation only, or dual-column bilingual. Ask about the book — AI Chat answers from the book itself, and citations jump back to the passage they came from, so you can check them. What you need A modern browser. A desktop browser gives you the full layouts, such as dual-column bilingual. No account needed to browse and read. Sign in when you want more. A small token allowance is included for trying AI Translation and AI Chat. You can also plug in your own model API key (BYOK). Next steps Sign In — accounts, social sign-in and guest reading Find Your First Book — browse the shelf, filter and search Reading Modes — choose the layout that suits you"},{"lang":"en","path":"translation/modes","title":"Translation Layouts","headings":["Translation Layouts","Interlinear","Translation only","Dual-column bilingual","Translation theme","Related pages"],"text":"Translation Layouts · FacetShelf Help Center Translation Layouts AI Translation can show the result in three ways, switched in the AI Translation section of reading settings. Interlinear The translation follows each source paragraph, original above and translation below in the same column. Good for checking sentence by sentence, or reading both texts together. Takes up more space than the original. Translation only Shows the translation alone; the original is no longer displayed. For when you only want to read the translation. Switch back to Interlinear whenever you need the original. Dual-column bilingual Original and translation side by side, with the two columns scrolling together. Best on a large screen. Dual-column total width sets the combined width; each column takes half. Translation theme The translated part can take a different visual theme — Default, Parchment or Thin border — so it is easy to tell apart from the original. Related pages Translation Scope & Languages Translate Selection"},{"lang":"en","path":"translation/scope-language","title":"Translation Scope & Languages","headings":["Translation Scope & Languages","Three ranges","Source and target language","Start translating","Related pages"],"text":"Translation Scope & Languages · FacetShelf Help Center Translation Scope & Languages First decide how much to translate, then what to translate it into. Three ranges RangeWhat happensGood for Translate while readingTranslates as you readReading only part of a book, or not waiting long Current chapterTranslates the whole current chapterReading one chapter straight through Whole bookTranslates the entire bookPlanning to read it from cover to cover The larger the range, the longer a single wait and the more it uses; try a small range first to judge the quality. Source and target language Source language — the book's own language, usually detected automatically. Target language — the language to translate into; it must differ from the source. Start translating Open a book and set the mode, range and target language in the AI Translation section. Click Start translating on the quick controls bar. The Translation Console in the right-hand panel shows progress. You can keep reading while it runs; translated parts appear as they arrive. Related pages Translation Layouts Quota & Usage"},{"lang":"en","path":"translation/selection","title":"Translate Selection","headings":["Translate Selection","How to use it","Character limit","How it differs from whole-book translation","Related pages"],"text":"Translate Selection · FacetShelf Help Center Translate Selection To understand one sentence or paragraph, you do not need to start a whole-book translation. How to use it Select the text you want translated in the book. Click Translate in the selection menu. The translation appears immediately. Character limit One request translates up to 4,000 characters. Anything longer is stopped locally with a message and no request is sent; select it in parts, or switch to chapter translation. How it differs from whole-book translation Translate SelectionWhole-book translation RangeThe passage you selectedTranslate while reading / current chapter / whole book Kept?A temporary result, not written into the bookShown with the book once translated Good forChecking a sentence, looking up a wordReading a paragraph, a chapter or the whole book Related pages Translation Layouts Notes & Annotations"}];
